sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task; DECISIONS R1 + round 2 websocket.sync (no Swamp run, the Gateway closes the task from Reverb's own reports). docs/reference/websocket-apps.md.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: websocket:app:create
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant N as Reverb<br/>on websocket Node
  CLI->>GW: websocket:app:create<br/>hauzer --operation-key=KEY
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit websocket:app:create hauzer`
  %%> - syntax: `<name> [--operation-key=KEY] [--json]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the app name: a lowercase kebab slug of at most 63 characters
  %%> - optionally an operation key, to retry the same request after a lost response
  %%> Who can call it:
  %%> - the `orbit` CLI and the MCP tool send the same request
  Note over GW: Save the app, revision 19<br/>R1: no run · task #5150
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - a Node has the `websocket` role
  %%> - the name is free and is not `gateway`; otherwise `validation.failed`
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - generates the app ID, key and secret; the secret is stored encrypted and never returned
  %%> - saves the app and a new registry revision 19 in one transaction
  %%> - records task #5150, which waits for revision 19
  %%> Why no Swamp run:
  %%> - nothing has to be done on a Node; Reverb pulls the registry itself (R1)
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the app exists in the Gateway; Reverb does not serve it yet
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5150 · app ID, key
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number, the app ID and the key, at once; never the secret
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
  loop each Reverb reconcile, 30 s
    N->>GW: Pull the registry<br/>full snapshot, revision 19
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - every Reverb process fetches the full registry snapshot on its own 30-second reconcile
    %%> - it adds the app without a restart; existing connections stay open
    %%> Not included:
    %%> - no Swamp step, no SSH and no Reverb restart
    N->>GW: Report applied revision<br/>per process and boot
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - each process reports the revision it applied, with its boot identity
    %%> Why:
    %%> - a report from an old boot cannot confirm a replacement process
  end
  alt every process applied 19
    Note over GW: Close the task<br/>succeeded · app served
    %%> Result:
    %%> - every serving Reverb process has loaded the app
    %%> - task #5150 succeeds
  else a later revision replaced it
    Note over GW: Close the task, failed<br/>websocket.registry_superseded
    %%> When:
    %%> - the app was destroyed or changed before every process applied revision 19
    %%> Result:
    %%> - task #5150 fails; the registry keeps its latest state
  else no fresh report in 5 min
    Note over GW: Close the task, failed<br/>websocket.registry_pending
    %%> When:
    %%> - a serving process is stale, missing or keeps failing to load the revision
    %%> Result:
    %%> - task #5150 fails; the saved app stays, and Reverb loads it when it recovers
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - run `websocket:sync` after the fix; it waits for the current revision
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5150
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
  end
